.TH VIMLEARN 1 "2026-11-11" "vimlearn" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vimlearn \- interactive ANSI terminal game for learning Vim keybindings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vimlearn
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vimlearn
is a cross-platform ANSI terminal puzzle and muscle-memory trainer for Vim keybindings.
It provides an interactive Vim primer tutorial, 25 handcrafted levels across five difficulty
tiers, and an Endless muscle-memory mode with four procedural training modes.
.PP
A minimum terminal size of
.B 80x24
is required to start and play.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tutorial
Launch directly into the 4-part interactive Vim Primer Tutorial.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List all difficulties, levels, Par scores, and objectives.
.TP
.BI "\-\-play " "difficulty level"
Start a specific difficulty and 1-based level number (for example:
.BR "--play hard 2" ).
.TP
.BI "\-\-endless " "difficulty " [ mode ]
Start Endless muscle-memory mode for
.I difficulty
using an optional sub-mode:
.BR random " (default), " multi ", " hunt ", or " rapid .
.TP
.B \-\-update
Check GitHub Releases for a newer release and install it.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Print the raw troff manual page to standard output (pipe to
.BR "man -l -" ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.SH DIFFICULTIES
.TP
.B beginner
Foundations:
.BR h ", " j ", " k ", " l ", " w ", " b ", " x ", " i ", " a ", " o ", " dd ", " u .
.TP
.B intermediate
Line anchors, character sniping, and repeat:
.BR 0 ", " ^ ", " $ ", " I ", " A ", " f ", " t ", " ; ", " dw ", " cw ", " yy ", " p ", " . .
.TP
.B hard
Counts, text objects, and search:
.BR 3j ", " 3dd ", " ci\(dq ", " da\(dq ", " ci( ", " di[ ", " gg ", " G ", " % ", " J ", " / ", " n ", " N .
.TP
.B expert
Surgical refactoring:
.BR v ", " V ", " ~ ", " r ", " ct) ", " dt) ", " ci{ ", " >> ", " << ", " ma ", " \(gaa .
.TP
.B impossible
Timed Vim Grandmaster challenges: macros
.RB ( qa ... q ", " @a ),
named registers
.RB ( \(dqay ", " \(dqap ),
nested text objects, and search-and-dot blitzes.
.SH ENDLESS MODES
Press
.B e
on any difficulty in the Home or Level Select screen to choose a training mode:
.TP
.B random
Alternates between Multi-Edit Mix, Code Hunt, and Rapid-Fire every round using an anti-repeat bag.
.TP
.B multi
Composable multi-step edits across realistic code and configuration snippets with streak escalation.
.TP
.B hunt
High-speed cursor navigation across highlighted tokens inside real code snippets.
.TP
.B rapid
Continuous Monkeytype-style micro-drills on a live buffer with Keys/sec tracking.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Menus
.TP
.BR j / k " or " Up / Down
Move selection.
.TP
.B Enter
Open selected difficulty or start selected level.
.TP
.B e
Open Endless Mode picker for the selected difficulty.
.TP
.B t
Open the Vim Primer Tutorial.
.TP
.B ?
Open the in-app Help & Controls overlay.
.TP
.BR Esc " or " q
Go back / quit.
.SS Gameplay (Inside Levels & Endless Mode)
.TP
.B Tab
Expand or collapse the full lesson and key hints panel (Normal mode).
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Toggle the step-by-step walkthrough and hint.
.TP
.B :help
Open the Help & Controls overlay without losing your buffer progress.
.TP
.B :reset
Restart the current level.
.TP
.B :q
Exit the current level or stop Endless Mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vimlearn/progress.json
Stores completed levels, best keystroke scores, star ratings, and Endless mode streaks.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/vimlearn.1
Manual page installed by
.BR install.sh .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vim (1)
